BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Find Your Vision: Creative iPhone Photography — Sebastopol Cente
 r For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260912T000000
DTEND:20260913T000000
UID:1e5429692777bd0e72700639f7da3963@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Find Your Vision: Creative iPhone Photography\n\n  \n    \n   
    \n        \n          $85.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, 
 September 12th\, 202612:00-4:00pm Your iPhone is more than a camera—it
 ’s a powerful creative tool that’s always with you. Whether you’re c
 apturing everyday moments\, family memories\, travel adventures\, or beaut
 iful landscapes\, your iPhone gives you the ability to create compelling p
 hotographs wherever you go.In this hands-on workshop\, you’ll discover h
 ow to unlock the full potential of your iPhone camera through practical de
 monstrations\, creative exercises\, and easy-to-understand instruction. We
 ’ll explore:Camera settings and controlsExposure\, focus\, and filtersSh
 utter speed and how to use each of your iPhone’s lenses effectivelyTechn
 iques for panoramas\, macro photography\, close-ups\, and portraitsSimple 
 compositional strategies that create stronger\, more engaging photographsB
 eyond the technical features\, we’ll focus on the artistic side of photo
 graphy—learning to see light\, recognize interesting compositions\, and 
 tell visual stories that make your images more meaningful and memorable.Wh
 at to BringYour iPhone\, a fully charged battery\, and your enthusiasm for
  learning and creativity!Android phones are welcome\, although demonstrati
 ons will be given on a newer iPhone. All iPhone models and every level of 
 photographic experience are welcome—from beginners to experienced photog
 raphers looking to see more creatively.You’ll leave with practical techn
 iques\, new creative ideas\, and a greater understanding of how to make ph
 otographs that go beyond snapshots. Whether you’re photographing people\
 , places\, travel\, or nature\, you’ll gain skills that will improve you
 r images and increase your enjoyment of photography.Please eat lunch befor
 e class.Join us and discover how to Find Your Vision while unlocking the c
 reative potential of the camera that’s always with you.About the Teacher
 : As a husband-and-wife team\, Susan and Neil Silverman have been “captu
 red” with photography for over 25 years - teaching\, leading workshops\,
  and working professionally with many venues. They have taught for the Kel
 by Photo Conferences\, Gualaa Arts Center\, Santa Rosa Junior College\, Pa
 cific Northwest Art School\, Point Reyes Field Institute\, Great American 
 Photography Workshop (GAPW)\, an Better Photo\, as well as many photo club
 s and organizations. Their work has been published both nationally and int
 ernationally. Sharing knowledge\, experiences\, and camaraderie is as impo
 rtant as “getting the shot”.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n        
         Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/find-your-vision-creative-iph
 one-photography
