SUMMARY:Art as Self-Discovery: Mixed Media Art — Sebastopol Center For t
 he Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260917T000000
DTEND:20260918T000000
UID:2a6d0bf537a52db359894736c439f519@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Art as Self-Discovery: Mixed Media Art\n\n  \n    \n      \n  
       \n          $285.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nArt as Self-Disco
 very: Mixed Media Art Thursdays\, 6:00-9:00pm\, September 17th\, 24th\, Oc
 tober 1st\, 8th Attendance: $275.00 + $10.00 Materials Fee In this 4 sessi
 on series\, students will explore the art of creating mixed-media art with
  multiple techniques. Marion will guide you through the basics of composit
 ion\, color theory\, and image selection. This workshop is designed for pe
 ople of all creative levels who wish to learn collage and mixed media skil
 ls\, connect with the community\, and engage in meaningful self-expression
 . Students will have access to a curated selection of collage materials\,
  paints\, and scissors\, and are encouraged to bring magazines and persona
 l images of choice. We will explore image selection and composition\, imag
 e transfer\, combining collage with acrylics and watercolors\, embedding 3
 D objects\, choosing mounting surfaces\, framing\, and more. Marion will o
 ffer individual and group guidance in each class. While we’ll appreciat
 e the aesthetic aspects of the work\, we will value the meaning and emotio
 nal resonance of each piece. This is a space for connection and non-judgem
 ent\, where your unique creative expression matters above all - inviting c
 uriosity and play to reveal new pathways of seeing and creating. Students
  are encouraged to bring the following materials: Gloves Preferred Glue
  Preferred scissorsAbout the Teacher: Marion Ruta Segal is Certified in C
 reative Arts Therapies  (The New School\, NYC) and practicing mixed media
  artist with nearly 20 years of teaching experience in New York City and t
 he San Francisco Bay Area. Her work includes painting\, collage\, and mixe
 d media\, and she has exhibited publicly since 2013. Marion has taught at 
 community organizations and at the college level\, leading workshops that 
 invite students into exploratory\, meaning-focused making - grounding them
  in core methods and aesthetics including design\, color theory\, and comp
 osition. She brings warmth\, depth\, and attunement to the studio\, helpin
 g participants feel comfortable and meeting them wherever they are creativ
 ely. Click here to learn more about Marion! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n           
