DESCRIPTION:Collage on Panel from Start to Finish - September 26th\n\n  \n
     \n      \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nS
 aturday\, September 26th\, 2026\; 11 AM - 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials fe
 eAge: 16+ Join French-American collage artist Catherine Cruz for a new com
 prehensive collage workshop designed to to guide you through the complete 
 process of creating a finished collage on wood panel. Her hands-on process
  will cover every step—from surface preparation and design to varnishing
  and wiring.  You will learn presentation tips to give your artwork a pro
 fessional finish. What you’ll obtain from this workshop:Reliable method
 s for preparing your panelTechnical information about selected art materia
 lsCreative ways to explore abstraction through collageTechniques for prese
 nting your artIMPORTANT: Each participant must purchase and bring the foll
 owing items:One 12”x12 cradled wood panel\, gallery style 1 ½” thickO
 ne roll of blue painter’s tape 2” wideOne small Phillips screw driver 
 (cross-shaped)IMPORTANT: Instructions for where to purchase your materials
  are provided in the attached PDF.  Each participant must purchase and b
 ring the items listed in the attached PDF.Materials provided by Instructor
 : a wide assortment of painted and printed collage papersbrushesacrylic me
 diumgessovarnishwiring suppliesscissorsThe class will begin with a demonst
 ration\, so please plan to arrive early to allow time to settle in.A short
  lunch break will be held from 12:30 to 1:00 PM. Kindly bring your own lun
 ch and beverage.About the instructor: Catherine Cruz is a French-American 
 artist whose work is informed by textures and patterns created by the pass
 ing of time and the effects of the natural elements on the built environme
 nt.  She holds a Bachelor of Science in interior design and she worked in
  the field of architectural design and green building certification for ov
 er 25 years.  She has taught collage and mixed media workshops in the Bay
  Area and in France since 2019\, and this is her fifth year at the Sebasto
 pol Center for the Arts.  Her studio is located in Sebastopol and she par
 ticipates in Art Trails Open Studios.  You may contact Catherine at beyou
 artstudio@gmail.com.  Check out Catherine’s other classes here:  https
 ://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
