BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Indonesian Batik: Wax\, Color & Storytelling — S
 ebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260928T000000
UID:c905f002342ac05b24c9b746cfada92c@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Introduction to Indonesian Batik: Wax\, Color & Storytelling\n
 \n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $120.00\n        \n      \n    \n 
  \n\nIntroduction to Indonesian Batik: Wax\, Color & Storytelling Sunday\
 , September 27th\, 2026 10:00am-1:00pm $95.00 + $25.00 Materials Fee = $
 120 Attendance Price Discover the beauty of Indonesian batik in this begi
 nner-friendly\, hands-on textile workshop. Batik is a traditional wax-resi
 st art form from Indonesia\, where wax is used to create patterns and prot
 ect areas of fabric before color is added.Students will begin with a short
  introduction to the cultural background and storytelling traditions of In
 donesian batik. Then\, step by step\, they will create their own small bat
 ik artwork on fabric using a traditional canting tool\, hot wax\, and fabr
 ic dyes. Participants may work from a simple provided design or develop th
 eir own motif with guidance.This class is designed to be creative\, relaxi
 ng\, and approachable for complete beginners as well as textile artists wh
 o want to explore a new process. All materials and tools will be provided\
 , and students will leave with their own handmade batik piece to take home
 .No previous drawing or batik experience is required. Because hot wax is u
 sed\, students will receive clear safety guidance throughout the workshop.
 About the Teacher: Theresia Debby Iriani is an Indonesian batik artist\, c
 lothing designer\, and founder of Oedel Batik\, a modern batik clothing li
 ne she has been developing since 2018. Since 2023\, Theresia has also open
 ed hands-on batik classes for guests visiting Bali\, and has led batik pai
 nting workshops for international visitors\, families\, children\, schools
 \, and corporate groups in Bali. Theresia’s classes introduce students t
 o the cultural background of Indonesian batik while guiding them through a
  hands-on process using traditional wax-resist techniques\, canting tools\
 , and fabric dyes. Theresia has experience adapting batik workshops for be
 ginners\, small creative groups\, and larger events. Theresia’s teaching
  style is warm\, step-by-step\, and focused on helping each participant fe
 el comfortable exploring their own design and creativity. Click here to se
 e more of Theresia’s work on her Instagram! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n          
     \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/introduction-to-indonesian-ba
 tik-wax-color-storytelling
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
