DESCRIPTION:Plein Air Watercolors at Ragle\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n
           $85.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nOnce a month on Saturdays:
  July 18th\, 202610:00am-2:00pm$75.00 + $10.00 materials fee In this singl
 e-session workshop\, participants will learn watercolor technique\, as wel
 l as the basics of painting landscapes from life. Students will choose a s
 cene to paint and receive instruction on composition\, color temperature a
 nd value\, and perspective. With a mixture of demonstrations and individu
 al instruction\, artists of all experience levels can learn something new 
 and have a positive creative encounter. Enjoy a day in our beautiful local
  park\, and gain a new appreciation for the beauty of your surroundings th
 rough close observation and careful rendering. Feel free to bring a plein
  air set up if you have one\, or a lightweight folding chair. Otherwise se
 ating is at picnic tables and park benches or on the ground. All other mat
 erials are provided. Location disclosed the day before the session in a we
 lcome email. About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Ar
 ts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from University of San Dieg
 o\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in prin
 tmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally shown and collected
 \, but her art practice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, and water
 color. She has taught all ages in many mediums. These days\, Hannah primar
 ily teaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, and paper cutting. You ca
 n view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
